## Independent handbook — lesson contents, part 1
otc.guide.page.placing_station.title=Set up a restaurant
otc.guide.page.placing_station.step1=Craft and place an order machine, menu board, countertop, chair, packaging shelf, plate shelf and washing sink.
otc.guide.page.placing_station.step2=Keep your work area within 24 blocks of the order machine. New order machines must be more than 24 blocks apart.
otc.guide.page.placing_station.step3=Place the packaging and plate shelves within five blocks of the countertop; preparation checks those supply distances.
otc.guide.page.first_menu.title=Choose starting dishes
otc.guide.page.first_menu.step1=A new menu board starts with four dishes. Hold a recognizable food and use the board to register another.
otc.guide.page.first_menu.step2=Menu registration does not consume food. Each dish adds its nutrition once, not once per item in the held stack.
otc.guide.page.first_menu.step3=Use the board empty-handed or while sneaking to manage dishes from your inventory. The menu holds up to 150 entries.
otc.guide.page.first_order.title=Fulfill your first order
otc.guide.page.first_order.step1=Start trading at the order machine, choose an offer and accept it. A normal order expires 30 minutes after creation.
otc.guide.page.first_order.step2=Obtain the finished dishes listed on the order, place them in your inventory or an accessible refrigerator, and prepare them at the countertop.
otc.guide.page.first_order.step3=Collect the plated meal or parcel from the countertop and use it on the matching customer. Payment and possible tips arrive on delivery.
otc.guide.page.guide_access.title=Read and replace the guide
otc.guide.page.guide_access.step1=You receive this separate Order To Cook handbook on first joining a world. Use it in your hand to open the contents.
otc.guide.page.guide_access.step2=Craft another guide with one book and one sheet of paper. It is not the Cookery guide or a replacement for it.
otc.guide.page.guide_access.step3=Browse main chapters, topics and lessons. Use Back, Previous and Next to continue reading.
otc.guide.page.menu_design.title=Manage the menu
otc.guide.page.menu_design.step1=Each menu entry is a finished dish, not a crafting recipe. The countertop cannot cook ingredients into a meal by itself.
otc.guide.page.menu_design.step2=Use a held food or the inventory picker. Special items without readable nutrition require an explicit food definition.
otc.guide.page.menu_design.step3=Remove and re-add an entry to adopt updated nutrition or names. Accepted orders keep their original requirements and price.
otc.guide.page.nutrition_variant.title=Nutrition and public variants
otc.guide.page.nutrition_variant.step1=Menu nutrition affects upgrades and income. A generic entry and a specific variant of the same item cannot double-count.
otc.guide.page.nutrition_variant.step2=When a food exposes Senluo V1 nativeVariant, variants can be ordered and matched individually. The wrong variant cannot fulfill the order.
otc.guide.page.nutrition_variant.step3=Quality, heat and seasoning are not separate menu identities or price multipliers. Legacy ID-only orders keep working.
otc.guide.page.offer_types.title=Understand order types
otc.guide.page.offer_types.step1=Dine-in orders use plates; delivery orders use parcels and have a destination.
otc.guide.page.offer_types.step2=Rush orders have shorter limits and long-distance deliveries travel farther. Walk-in customers require a usable chair.
otc.guide.page.offer_types.step3=Accepting one machine offer cancels its alternatives, but independent walk-in requests remain.
otc.guide.page.timers.title=Timing and expiration
otc.guide.page.timers.step1=New machine offers refresh every ten minutes by default. Normal orders last 30 minutes; rush orders last ten.
otc.guide.page.timers.step2=The clock starts when an order is generated, not accepted. In this version real-time deadlines still pass while away.
otc.guide.page.timers.step3=Expired orders cannot be delivered. A refresh does not erase accepted work or already packed orders.
otc.guide.page.money_upgrades.title=Coins and restaurant upgrades
otc.guide.page.money_upgrades.step1=Completed orders pay oTc coins and possible tips. Lifetime earnings are not spendable wallet balance.
otc.guide.page.money_upgrades.step2=The order machine shows the cost and menu nutrition required for the next upgrade, from level 0 up to level 8.
otc.guide.page.money_upgrades.step3=Insufficient nutrition blocks an upgrade. Removing dishes does not erase a purchased level but can lower its benefits.
otc.guide.page.staff.title=Owners and staff
otc.guide.page.staff.step1=The player who places the order machine owns the restaurant and can add staff in its settings.
otc.guide.page.staff.step2=Preparation and refrigerator access recheck permissions. An old open form cannot bypass a later revocation.
otc.guide.page.staff.step3=Do not break active equipment with outstanding orders, plates or pending records. Stop trading and clean up first.
otc.guide.page.countertop.title=Countertop and ingredient handling
otc.guide.page.countertop.step1=The countertop uses finished dishes from your inventory or accessible refrigerators within 24 blocks.
otc.guide.page.countertop.step2=Keep the matching supply shelf within five blocks and the space above the countertop clear before preparing an order.
otc.guide.page.countertop.step3=Items and supplies are debited only when the full requirement matches. Collect the finished meal from the countertop.
otc.guide.page.supplies.title=Packaging and plate shelves
otc.guide.page.supplies.step1=Delivery uses leather from the packaging shelf; dining uses clean plates from the plate shelf. Both must be within five blocks.
otc.guide.page.supplies.step2=The packaging shelf holds ten units; the plate shelf holds 18. Use the matching item on the shelf to refill it.
otc.guide.page.supplies.step3=Dirty plates are not clean supplies. Wash them in a sink or dishwasher before restocking the plate shelf.
otc.guide.page.refrigerator.title=Refrigerator compartments
otc.guide.page.refrigerator.step1=The refrigerator has separate upper (27 slots) and lower (54 slots) compartments with independent door access.
otc.guide.page.refrigerator.step2=A nearby authorized refrigerator can supply the countertop. Stack limits follow Bedrock, not Java's 128 items per slot.
otc.guide.page.refrigerator.step3=The upgrade box can convert an eligible empty double barrel into a refrigerator. Check both blocks and inventories first.
otc.guide.page.stove.title=Three-lane stove and fuel
otc.guide.page.stove.step1=The stove has three cooking lanes and needs a recognized fuel and compatible ingredients.
otc.guide.page.stove.step2=Nine explicit vanilla smoking conversions are supported, such as raw beef to cooked beef. It does not automatically import other add-ons' recipes.
otc.guide.page.stove.step3=The upgrade box can convert an eligible empty smoker. Senluo skewers still belong to their own cooking stations.
